   "text": "I read the macrocycle as a linear chain of residues that closes back on itself, and wrote the SMILES by tracing that ring from the N-methyl cyclopentylglycine nitrogen.\n\n**Ring sequence (clockwise from the top left):**\n1. N-methyl cyclopentylglycine.\n2. N-methyl aspartic acid with its side-chain carboxyl as the amide to azepane. Its \u03b1-carboxyl is the morpholine amide.\n3. Azepane-2-carboxylic acid (the azepane ring is the cyclic amine of the previous residue).\n4. Isoleucine, drawn with the L configuration at both the \u03b1 and \u03b2 carbons.\n5. Sarcosine.\n6. Sarcosine.\n7. N-propyl 4-(trifluoromethyl)phenylalanine.\n8. Sarcosine.\n9. Homophenylalanine bearing a 3-chloro-4-(trifluoromethyl)phenyl group on the chain.\n10. Proline.\n11. 1-Aminocyclopentane-1-carboxylic acid, which closes the ring back to residue 1.\n\n**Stereochemistry:** I assigned each stereocentre from its wedge or hash bond:\n- Cyclopentylglycine \u03b1-carbon: wedge to the cyclopentyl group.\n- Aspartic acid \u03b1-carbon: wedge to the morpholine carbonyl.\n- Azepane C2: wedge to the ring CH2.\n- Isoleucine \u03b2-carbon: wedge to the methyl group.\n- N-propyl phenylalanine \u03b1-carbon: hash to the benzyl CH2.\n- Homophenylalanine \u03b1-carbon: hash to the chain CH2.\n- Proline \u03b1-carbon: wedge to the ring CH2.\n\nThe isoleucine \u03b1-carbon is the least certain, because I could not tell which end of its wedge is narrow. I took the wedge as pointing toward the NH, which gives the natural L-isoleucine configuration.\n\nSMILES: CN1[C@@H](C2CCCC2)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](C(=O)N2CCOCC2)CC(=O)N2CCCCC[C@H]2C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)CC)C(=O)N(C)CC(=O)N(C)CC(=O)N(CCC)[C@H](Cc2ccc(C(F)(F)F)cc2)C(=O)N(C)CC(=O)N[C@H](CCc2ccc(C(F)(F)F)c(Cl)c2)C(=O)N2CCC[C@H]2C(=O)NC2(CCCC2)C(=O)1"
  }
